post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

  ZT9101 (LV-UW03) driver installed.

  * pacman's DKMS hook compiles and signs the module for every installed
    kernel that has headers. If you saw a warning such as

        Missing <kernel> kernel headers for module zt9101/<version>.

    then install headers for the kernel you boot and finish the build:

        sudo pacman -S linux-headers          # linux
        sudo pacman -S linux-cachyos-headers  # linux-cachyos
        sudo pacman -S linux-lts-headers      # linux-lts
        sudo dkms autoinstall

  * If the adapter is already plugged in, unplug it and plug it back in
    (or reboot). udev only learns that a driver now exists for it when the
    device is enumerated.

  * No init-system configuration was installed. The module autoloads from
    its USB modalias through udev's 80-drivers.rules, which ships with both
    systemd-udev and eudev -- so this works on Arch, Artix (OpenRC, s6,
    runit, dinit) and CachyOS alike, with nothing to configure.

  Check status with:

        dkms status | grep zt9101
        ip link show wlan0

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'

  ZT9101 (LV-UW03) driver removed. Unplug and replug the adapter, or
  reboot, to release it.

EOF
}
